Approach: Use Floyd’s Cycle Detection (Tortoise and Hare). Move slow by one step and fast by two steps; if they meet, a cycle exists, otherwise reach null.

Time Complexity: O(n) — in the worst case, the pointers traverse the linked list once before meeting or reaching the end.

Space Complexity: O(1) — only two pointer variables are used, no extra data structures.

public class Solution {
    public boolean hasCycle(ListNode head) {
        ListNode slow=head,fast=head;
        while(fast!=null && fast.next!=null){
            slow=slow.next;
            fast=fast.next.next;
            if(slow==fast){
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;
    }
}
